    "description": "<p>This is the reader-facing Emmy Noether working record for the Modern LaTeX Editions of Mathematics Manuscripts project. It contains modern LaTeX working editions, source-control material, and multilingual working translations; it is not a critical edition.</p><p><strong>German and English:</strong> the record continues to front the 466-page v26/R823 German source-control reader. It retains the inherited RA10 English cumulative reader, standalone English Papers 01-43, and twelve bounded English components synchronized to R823. The full English reader is not globally synchronized to R823.</p><p><strong>Spanish:</strong> the 473-page Spanish R823 working translation covers all 81 declared source units, Papers 01-43, all 31 lecture-book sections, and retained terminal material. Its declared source-reconciliation gate passed, but this is not native-language or peer-review certification.</p><p><strong>Interslavic:</strong> two directly readable working-translation PDFs expose 221 canonical Latin-script units as a 529-page reader and 221 paired Cyrillic-script units as a 552-page reader. File <code>11</code> groups the complete current TeX bodies, all individual PDFs, unit mapping, support metadata, normalization preimages/diffs/ledgers, build logs, scripts, and visual-QA evidence. Orthography Tranche 002A changed 146 files; exact lexical Tranche 002B changed 92 files. Both transformations passed idempotence checks and preserved held or unreviewed forms. The archive pass compiled all 442 canonical units with no missing-character or box-overflow diagnostics; four symmetric <code>amsmath</code> bracket-group notices remain in Paper 06 sections 02-03.</p><p><strong>Other material:</strong> the record retains bounded CJK/Korean components, the earlier Paper 06 Slavic tranche, German source packages, source-repair/audit material, and grouped multilingual checkpoints.</p><p><strong>Status caveat:</strong> these are substantial machine-produced working editions and translations. They are not a critical edition, native-language or community certification, peer review, publication-grade final edition, complete multilingual synchronization, or a guarantee that every word, formula, diagram, and symbol has received independent human source verification. Build and render checks establish artifact integrity and bounded change control; they do not establish linguistic or mathematical correctness.</p><p><strong>GitHub:</strong> corrections, source comparisons, LaTeX fixes, and translation improvements can be suggested through issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
    "additional_descriptions": [
      {
        "description": "Reader-first public surface: R823 German source-control, RA10 and bounded R823 English, 473-page Spanish R823, and 529/552-page Interslavic Latin/Cyrillic working readers. Not a critical edition, native-language certification, peer review, or complete source-level multilingual synchronization.",
