    "description_stripped": "This is the reader-facing Emmy Noether working record for the Modern LaTeX Editions of Mathematics Manuscripts project. It contains modern LaTeX working editions, source-control material, and multilingual working translations; it is not a critical edition.\nGerman and English: the record continues to front the 466-page v26/R823 German source-control reader. It retains the inherited RA10 English cumulative reader, standalone English Papers 01-43, and twelve bounded English components synchronized to R823. The full English reader is not globally synchronized to R823.\nSpanish: the 473-page Spanish R823 working translation covers all 81 declared source units, Papers 01-43, all 31 lecture-book sections, and retained terminal material. Its declared source-reconciliation gate passed, but this is not native-language or peer-review certification.\nInterslavic: two directly readable working-translation PDFs expose 221 canonical Latin-script units as a 529-page reader and 221 paired Cyrillic-script units as a 552-page reader. File 11 groups the complete current TeX bodies, all individual PDFs, unit mapping, support metadata, normalization preimages/diffs/ledgers, build logs, scripts, and visual-QA evidence. Orthography Tranche 002A changed 146 files; exact lexical Tranche 002B changed 92 files. Both transformations passed idempotence checks and preserved held or unreviewed forms. The archive pass compiled all 442 canonical units with no missing-character or box-overflow diagnostics; four symmetric amsmath bracket-group notices remain in Paper 06 sections 02-03.\nOther material: the record retains bounded CJK/Korean components, the earlier Paper 06 Slavic tranche, German source packages, source-repair/audit material, and grouped multilingual checkpoints.\nStatus caveat: these are substantial machine-produced working editions and translations. They are not a critical edition, native-language or community certification, peer review, publication-grade final edition, complete multilingual synchronization, or a guarantee that every word, formula, diagram, and symbol has received independent human source verification. Build and render checks establish artifact integrity and bounded change control; they do not establish linguistic or mathematical correctness.\nGitHub: corrections, source comparisons, LaTeX fixes, and translation improvements can be suggested through issues or pull requests at https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts.",
    "version": "2026-07-18 R823 German and Spanish with normalized Interslavic working readers",
